@opinion_archive
title: Public mood
new-page: true
is-special: true
call: status

= Public mood

<div class="ledger-section ledger-section-first"><div class="ledger-title">National pressure</div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Panic / issue pressure</span><b>[+ status_public_panic +]/100</b></div>
<div class="ledger-subrow">[+ status_public_panic_band +] · hottest field: [+ status_public_hottest +]</div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Cross-issue consensus</span><b>[+ status_public_consensus +]/100</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Legacy-event pressure this month</span><b>[+ status_public_bridge_pressure +]/100</b></div>
<div class="ledger-subrow">Updated [+ status_public_updated +]</div></div>

<div class="ledger-section"><div class="ledger-title">Latent attitudes</div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Acceptance of capitalism and market hierarchy</span><b>[+ status_capitalism_acceptance +]/100</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Expectation of transfers and public services</span><b>[+ status_welfare_expectation +]/100</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Cultural conservatism</span><b>[+ status_cultural_conservatism +]/100</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Order and threat sensitivity</span><b>[+ status_order_threat_sensitivity +]/100</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Universal solidarity</span><b>[+ status_universal_solidarity +]/100</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Institutional trust</span><b>[+ status_institutional_trust +]/100</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Appetite for political change</span><b>[+ status_change_appetite +]/100</b></div>
<div class="ledger-note">These values are independent. Welfare expectation is not socialist identification, and a culturally conservative voter may strongly favour pensions, family benefits and public healthcare.</div></div>

<div class="ledger-section"><div class="ledger-title">Latest story contest</div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>[+ status_story_last_title +]</span><b>signal [+ status_story_last_signal +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-subrow">Reach [+ status_story_last_reach +] × audience trust [+ status_story_last_audience_trust +] × frame [+ status_story_last_frame +] × messenger [+ status_story_last_messenger_credibility +] × salience [+ status_story_last_issue_salience +] × Left credibility [+ status_story_last_left_credibility +]</div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Persuasion · backlash</span><b>[+ status_story_persuasion +] · [+ status_story_backlash +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Mobilisation · abstention</span><b>[+ status_story_mobilisation +] · [+ status_story_abstention +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Issue ownership</span><b>[+ status_story_issue_ownership +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-subrow">Field: [+ status_story_last_issue +]</div>
<div class="ledger-subrow">Memory: salience [+ status_story_salience_memory +] · distrust [+ status_story_distrust_memory +] · backlash [+ status_story_backlash_memory +] · reputation [+ status_story_reputation_memory +]</div></div>

<div class="ledger-section"><div class="ledger-title">Lewica historical pressure</div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Electoral viability · winner reputation</span><b>[+ status_electoral_viability +] · [+ status_winner_reputation +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Issue ownership · media access</span><b>[+ status_issue_ownership +] · [+ status_media_access +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Leadership authority · list confidence</span><b>[+ status_leadership_authority +] · [+ status_list_confidence +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Coalition blur</span><b>[+ status_coalition_blur +]/100</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Tactical loss: KO · abstention · PL2050</span><b>[+ status_tactical_desertion_to_ko +] · [+ status_tactical_desertion_to_abstention +] · [+ status_tactical_desertion_to_p2050 +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-subrow">[+ status_historical_pressure_last +]</div>
<div class="ledger-note">Benchmarks: 12.56% (2019), 2.22% presidential (2020), 8.61% (2023), 4.23% Biejat and 4.86% Zandberg (2025). Pressure is hostile but organisation, delivery and credible differentiation can reverse it.</div></div>

<div class="ledger-section"><div class="ledger-title">Movement and migration trajectories</div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Women's Strike: activists · sympathy</span><b>[+ status_womens_strike_activist_mobilisation +] · [+ status_womens_strike_public_sympathy +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Party conversion · conservative backlash</span><b>[+ status_womens_strike_party_conversion +] · [+ status_womens_strike_conservative_backlash +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Migration: empathy · border competence</span><b>[+ status_migration_empathy +] · [+ status_migration_border_competence +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Local services · welfare competition · disinformation</span><b>[+ status_migration_local_service_capacity +] · [+ status_migration_welfare_competition +] · [+ status_migration_disinformation +]</b></div></div>

<div class="ledger-section"><div class="ledger-title">Rights, family and church</div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Abortion rights</span><b>[+ status_abortion_rights_support +] · [+ status_abortion_rights_salience +] · [+ status_abortion_rights_backlash +]</b></div>
